Ref: fin.sales_invoice_history.(workspace_id, sales_invoice_id) > fin.sales_invoice.(workspace_id, sales_invoice_id)
Ref: fin.sales_invoice_history.(workspace_id, performer_contact_id) > pc.contact.(workspace_id, contact_id) [color: #9ca3af]

// =====================================================================
// T24 · decisions, the hand-over to the engine repo, and what stays open (rev 14)
// =====================================================================
// D1  The AE books the accounting voucher; Billing raises the invoice (Vijay, 18-Nov). Billing's invoice tables are Billing's (G37).
// D2  Manoj's model, mirrored (Vijay, 18-Nov, rev 14): one voucher table + its lines + its history per voucher type; ONE shared
//     book (fin.journal_entry / fin.journal_line). Rev 13's common fin.voucher (+ voucher_gst, voucher_line, voucher_history,
//     posting_rule) is withdrawn; G38 is closed by following his design.
// D3  Never booked twice: the EXCLUDE above (Billing's invoice number per GSTIN per year) + journal_entry_one_forward_entry_per_document.
// D4  The ledgers are suggested by the rules R1–R12 in code (as his R1–R6), the AE may pick others; nothing about the suggestion
//     is stored (as his). The Accounts Manager sees the rule's suggestion recomputed beside the lines (the app's "Rule · why").
// D5  Stages as his: submitted → posted | rejected | draft (sent back) → submitted; posted → amended (by an approved amendment).
// D6  Approve = every gate again, then PostJournalEntry in one transaction. The customer line posts to its account's ledger
//     naming the account (no control ledger); a picked other receivable ledger is G36.
// D7  No stored balances: what a customer owes = Σ(debit − credit) of its journal lines; the due date is on the voucher.
// D8  Return to Billing (the app's button) writes no row here: it is a message back to Billing (G37), whose invoice it is.
//
// D9  Rev 15 (Vijay, 20-Nov): the cost of goods sold comes from inventory, on the same voucher and entry (rule R13). The method
//     (FIFO | weighted average) is a company setting (G3); the voucher keeps the one used (costing_method). LIFO: not allowed.
//     Stock goes down at Approve, in the same transaction as PostJournalEntry. Σ value of the lots = the 106020 balance (T9).
//
// HAND-OVER: what migration 0007 (after his 0006) must do, in order:
//   1  fin.sales_invoice (with the 2 GENERATED columns), fin.sales_invoice_line, fin.sales_invoice_history: CHECKs and indexes
//      above; the never-twice EXCLUDE and the partial index by hand (as his 0005).
//   2  ALTER fin.journal_entry: voucher_type CHECK + 'sales'. ALTER fin.ledger_account: account types output_cgst, output_sgst,
//      output_igst, tcs_payable (round_off is his, 0006).
//   3  Seeds: the sales and output GST ledgers (401010–401030 CA ✓; 206011–206014, 108030, 109040, 110030, 206040, 401050, 401070
//      proposed, G18) · 107020–107130 receivable ledgers and each debtor category on its own (his seed points all 16 at 107010, G28).
//   4  Triggers as his: clocks on fin.sales_invoice; append-only on fin.sales_invoice_history; pc.isolate_by_workspace on all 3.
//   5  Code: capabilities/finance/sales_invoice.py (submit, decide: his purchase_invoice.py, customer side) on journal.post_journal_entry,
//      + journal.debtor_balance (the twin of creditor_balance); the rules R1–R12 propose the lines (his supplier_invoice.propose).
//   6  Rev 15: schema inv + inv.stock_lot (a stub until the inventory module, T8 / S4); seed 501040 Cost of Goods Sold (proposed)
//      and 106020 Finished Goods (account_type stock); R13 reads the lots by the method; Approve lowers quantity_left (and, under
//      weighted average, rewrites unit_cost to value left ÷ quantity left) in the posting transaction.
// TO AGREE WITH MANOJ (G28): his placeholder codes clash with the CA's chart (Indian GAAP sheet): 2010nn payables (CA 201010 =
//   Term Loans; CA payables are 205010–205180) · 103010/103020 stock (CA = Goodwill / Computer Software; CA stock 106010–106030) ·
//   108010–108030 Input GST (CA = Cash in Hand / Bank; CA GST input 109030) · 203010 TDS Payable (CA = Provision for Gratuity) ·
//   501010–501030 expenses (CA = Raw Material Consumed / Purchase – Traded Goods / Change in Inventory). One chart: the CA's.

// =====================================================================
// Rev 15 · the inventory the cost comes from (a ROUGH STUB: not accounting; the inventory module owns it, T8 / S4, G3)
// =====================================================================

Table inv.stock_lot [headercolor: #7C3AED] {
  stock_lot_id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  workspace_id text [not null]
  branch_id uuid [not null, note: 'the branch holding it: KA-01']
  godown_code text [not null, note: 'KA-FG (finished goods)']
  item_code text [not null, note: 'FG-101 Glucose biscuit (the item master is in code until T8, G20)']
  lot_no text [not null, note: 'the batch: G-2604']
  received_on date [not null, note: 'FIFO order: the oldest goes out first. 14-Apr-2026 (illustrative)']
  quantity_received "numeric(18,3)" [not null, note: '300']
  quantity_left "numeric(18,3)" [not null, note: '300 → 0 after B4-01 (FIFO)']
  unit_cost "numeric(18,4)" [not null, note: '₹540.0000 (illustrative). Weighted average: rewritten to the average after each issue']
  recorded_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  checks {
    `quantity_received > 0` [name: 'stock_lot_quantity_received_positive']
    `quantity_left >= 0 AND quantity_left <= quantity_received` [name: 'stock_lot_quantity_left_in_range']
    `unit_cost >= 0` [name: 'stock_lot_unit_cost_not_negative']
  }
  Indexes {
    (workspace_id, stock_lot_id) [unique, name: 'stock_lot_workspace_identity_key']
    (workspace_id, branch_id, godown_code, item_code, lot_no) [unique, name: 'stock_lot_lot_key']
    (workspace_id, branch_id, item_code, received_on) [name: 'stock_lot_fifo_idx', note: 'FIFO: the oldest lot with stock left first']
  }
  Note: '''Rev 15: one row per lot received. Where the cost of goods sold comes from: FIFO takes the oldest lots, each at its own
unit_cost; weighted average takes Σ(quantity_left × unit_cost) ÷ Σ quantity_left. A ROUGH STUB for the demo: the inventory
module (receipts, issues, batches, its own history) replaces it (T8 / S4, G3). Σ(quantity_left × unit_cost) = the balance of
106020 Finished Goods (the T9 reconciliation).'''
}

Ref: inv.stock_lot.(workspace_id, branch_id) > fin.branch.(workspace_id, branch_id)

